cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SlangImage in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "SlangImage: cross-platform GPU image processing on Slang/slangpy"
abstract: >-
  SlangImage is a cross-platform GPU image-processing library built on Slang and
  slangpy — one kernel codebase running on Metal, CUDA, and Vulkan, fp16-first,
  with differentiable ops for PyTorch (including a learnable color-grading LUT).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tatar
    given-names: Tekin
  - name: "BeFunky, Inc."
repository-code: "https://github.com/tekintatar/slangimage"
url: "https://github.com/tekintatar/slangimage"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.1
keywords:
  - image-processing
  - gpu
  - slang
  - slangpy
  - cuda
  - metal
  - vulkan
  - pytorch
  - differentiable
